FUNCTION: The convergence process. This runs every time a group of agents is
spawned together. The agents hold a group conversation about how to accomplish a
shared goal and drive toward one answer.

- Every agent inherits the same conversation (the INPUT) but is given its own
  PURPOSE (its AGENT_TYPE angle on the project).
- Each round, every agent forms a response — either a plan or a prototype/execution
  ("please give the most appropriate response at this level of the project, either
  plan or execute"). Every response is aggregated and fed back into every agent.
- After the work response, every agent is asked to vote. The vote is collected by
  a simple text match for "I vote FINISHED" or "I vote INCOMPLETE"; the vote must
  be the final word of the agent's message.
- When EVERY agent votes FINISHED, the convergence is complete and its result is
  handed off to the zipper process.
- If ANY agent votes INCOMPLETE, the collective reasoning is consolidated and fed
  back to every agent for a reassessment, and the vote round repeats.

AGENT INITIATION: Don't be pushed around, stand your ground and only agree when
it's reasonable to do so. Your job is to work together with the other agents to
deliver a finished project.
